    fix: align documented runtime behavior. Addresses DOC-18
    
    Correct the required-key guidance, video-maker usage, and architecture model
    routing claims against the current command and source surfaces. Remove the
    legacy game-loop constructor catch that advertised an unreachable no-key stub
    mode while preserving later runtime decision fallback behavior.
    
    Add focused coverage for the real no-key VisionClient failure and for
    propagation of AI-manager constructor errors.
    
    Guard override: the repository hook unconditionally blocks staged .env.example
    as a sensitive-path class even though DOC-18 requires that tracked template.
    Its full-suite run also hit the unrelated, reproducible dashboard test
    TestScreenshotsLatest::test_with_auth_no_screenshots_returns_404 because the
    fixture creates its request after dependency patches end and sees the preserved
    prior-tick game_saves/screenshots files. The test fails identically standalone;
    DOC-18 focused tests, ruff, and mypy pass. The foreman will run GitReins after
    this commit as required by the owning row.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
